		title = "Feathers and Classes",
		text = "People who work for a Wing are called Feathers. Inside a Wing, staff hold numbered Classes, and the numbers count upward: Class 1 is the bottom, and Class 5 is treated as very senior. An old joke says it depends on the Wing, and that somewhere there's a Wing with a Class 20.\n\nAbove the Classes sit Directors, and above them each Wing's own kind of ruler: a Chief Executive Director in T Corp, a King with his retainers in S Corp, a Family Hierarch in H Corp. Feathers get good pay, a badge that opens checkpoints and a shot at Nest residence. What they don't get is an easy way out. A feather doesn't fall from its Wing of its own will.",
